{"data":{"actorId":"01KSPWEZWS89N7M7Y97XMXP6JV","createdAt":"2026-08-20T18:19:10.622Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"25","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Addressed in 878027a2f. The swept case now has its own branch with a Debug log, so it is distinguishable from the read-error fallback. Treating swept-as-ended is deliberately NOT the fix: freshState == nil means the sweeper (finalizeExitedSessions or endSessionNow) removed the state, and both condense as part of ending the session — the just-completed record is materialized by whoever removed it. Condensing here instead would either duplicate that work or operate on state that no longer exists.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M0G4KCP58ANF6N5DFNPRSB1E","targetId":"01M0G4KCPC273KKVAGJZ2KME1E","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M09WK1QC1B0BRSSR8G284MJX"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
